@startuml
 title GroupWave — отправка и доставка сообщения
 autonumber
 actor "Отправитель" as Sender
 participant "Realtime Gateway" as RT
 participant "Message Service" as Msg
 participant "Chat Service" as Chat
 database "DynamoDB" as DDB
 participant "DynamoDB Streams Relay" as Relay
 queue "Kafka" as Kafka
 participant "Delivery Worker" as Worker
 participant "Presence Service" as Presence
 participant "Gateway получателя" as RT2
 participant "Push Service" as Push

 Sender -> RT : WSS message.send(clientMessageId, chatId, text)
 RT -> Msg : validate + persist command
 Msg -> Chat : check membership / write permission
 Chat --> Msg : allowed
 Msg -> DDB : conditional write (dedup by clientMessageId)
 DDB --> Msg : committed / existing message
 Msg --> RT : message.accepted(messageId, cursor)
 RT --> Sender : WSS ACK after durable write

 DDB --> Relay : stream record after commit
 Relay -> Kafka : message.persisted(eventId, chatId, messageId)
 Kafka -> Worker : consume event (at-least-once)
 Worker -> Chat : get active member IDs
 Chat --> Worker : member list
 loop each recipient user/device
   Worker -> Presence : lookup active gateway
   alt active WSS connection
     Presence --> Worker : gatewayId
     Worker -> RT2 : internal deliver(messageId)
     RT2 --> Worker : accepted for socket write
   else offline / no route
     Worker -> Kafka : enqueue push.jobs (if not muted)
   end
 end
 Kafka -> Push : consume push.jobs
 Push --> Sender : (provider sends to recipient device) push notification
 note over Worker,Kafka
   Delivery is at-least-once. Consumer and client deduplicate by eventId/messageId.
   History sync via REST repairs gaps after reconnect.
 end note
@enduml
